<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [915].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>915&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;SEMI-SOLID AUTOTROPHIC GROWTH MEDIUM FOR MAGNETOCOCCUS MARINUS</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NaCl                                                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;16.4&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> MgCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;6H<sub>2</sub>O                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;3.49&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Na<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>                                             </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.74&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> KCl                                                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.47&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> CaCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;2H<sub>2</sub>O                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.39&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NH<sub>4</sub>Cl                                                 </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Modified Wolfe's mineral solution (see below)            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.4&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                          </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Agarose                                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g   </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly, except agar, and adjust pH to 7.0.  Add agarose to the medium and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub> gas atmosphere.  After cooling to 50C, add the following solutions to the medium aseptically and anaerobically (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized):    <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 0.5 M Potassium phosphate buffer (pH 7.0)                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.8&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 40% Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>&#183;5H<sub>2</sub>O solution             </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;3.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Vitamin solution* (see below)                            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% L-Cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O solution          </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;4.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution*                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.35&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Keep the medium temperature at 50C until the medium is distributed into sterile screw-capped test tubes as described below.  <br>
Adjust pH to 7.0 - 7.2 with sterile HCl or NaOH solution.  Then, aseptically and anaerobically, add the following solution (autoclaved):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 0.01 M FeSO<sub>4</sub>&#183;5H<sub>2</sub>Osolution (in 0.02 N HCl)    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Dispense the medium to sterile screw-capped test tubes (typically 12 ml medium into 125 by 15 mm test tubes) under air and cap.  Allow to stand until the medium is solidified and a O<sub>2</sub>-gradient formed (as evidenced by a pink upper oxic zone and a colorless lower anoxic zone).  Inoculate cells just below the pink-colorless interface in the medium tube using a syringe.  <br>
<I>Modified Wolfe's mineral solution:</I> <br>
Use trace minerals (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=151">151</a>) with final 0.4 g/L Na<sub>2</sub>MoO<sub>4</sub>&#183;2H<sub>2</sub>O, 0.02 g/L CuSO<sub>4</sub>&#183;5H<sub>2</sub>O and 0.01 g/L NiCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;6H<sub>2</sub>O.  <br>
<I>Vitamin solution:</I> <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Thiamine&#183;HCl                                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;90.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> <I>myo</I>-Inositol                                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;40.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Calcium pantothenate                                     </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;4.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> <I>p</I>-Aminobenzoic acid                              </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Vitamin B<sub>1</sub><sub>2</sub>                                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Pyridoxine&#183;HCl                                     </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;4.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Nicotinic acid                                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;4.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Biotin                                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Folic acid                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;100.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Comment: The medium tubes can be stocked under a N<sub>2</sub> gas atmosphere. In this case, prior to use, fill the head space with air and allow to stand until the O<sub>2</sub> gradient is formed.       <br>
